Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test(sim): pin the arc split with a wide tool's helical
 entry (#4179)

An ordinary arc never passes the per-move ceiling: its pieces are capped
at a quarter turn with the sagitta under the chord tolerance. A 127 mm
flat tool's steep helical entry does, so this pin fails on main (the
field engine refuses the helix) and passes with `ArcPiece::split`.

A helical piece is searched cell by cell, about 22 min in debug, so the
test runs in the heavy lane (`#[ignore]`, `--release -- --ignored`).
